{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "04_interactive_charts_and_tables",
    "course": "BlaiseNotebook Masterclass",
    "lesson": 4,
    "title": "Interactive Visualizations & Data Tables",
    "framework": "BlaiseVue",
    "engine": "Synopse mORMot 2 + Free Pascal",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_1_charts_intro",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# 📈 Example 4: Interactive Visualizations & Data Tables\n\nNumbers tell a story, but charts make that story clear! BlaiseNotebook includes built-in support for **Chart.js (`<bv-chart>`)** and **responsive data tables** that render directly below your code.\n\n### 🎯 In this lesson, you will learn:\n1. How to render smooth line charts with `ShowChart`.\n2. How to create multi-dataset bar charts with custom colors.\n3. How to display responsive, scrollable tables with `ShowTable`.\n4. How users can hover over charts to inspect exact values."
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_2_code_line_chart",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "// 1. Rendering a Smooth Line Chart with Chart.js\nbegin\n  Writeln('Generating 6-month revenue trend chart...');\n\n  ShowChart(\n    'Monthly Revenue Trend (2026)',\n    'line',\n    '{\"labels\": [\"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Apr\", \"May\", \"Jun\"],'#10 +\n    ' \"datasets\": [{'#10 +\n    '   \"label\": \"Revenue ($k)\",'#10 +\n    '   \"data\": [45.2, 52.8, 68.1, 74.5, 88.0, 105.4],'#10 +\n    '   \"borderColor\": \"#3b82f6\",'#10 +\n    '   \"backgroundColor\": \"rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.2)\",'#10 +\n    '   \"tension\": 0.35,'#10 +\n    '   \"fill\": true'#10 +\n    ' }]}' \n  );\nend;"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_3_md_bar_chart_note",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 📊 Multi-Dataset Bar Charts\n\nYou can compare multiple categories side-by-side using bar charts. Notice how the JSON payload specifies different colors (`#10b981` emerald, `#f59e0b` amber) for each dataset:"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_4_code_bar_chart",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "// 2. Multi-Dataset Bar Chart: Projected vs Actual Sales\nbegin\n  ShowChart(\n    'Quarterly Sales Comparison (Target vs Actual)',\n    'bar',\n    '{\"labels\": [\"Q1\", \"Q2\", \"Q3\", \"Q4\"],'#10 +\n    ' \"datasets\": ['#10 +\n    '   {\"label\": \"Target Goal\", \"data\": [100, 120, 140, 180], \"backgroundColor\": \"#94a3b8\"},'#10 +\n    '   {\"label\": \"Actual Achieved\", \"data\": [112, 135, 138, 205], \"backgroundColor\": \"#10b981\"}'#10 +\n    ' ]}'\n  );\nend;"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_5_code_data_table",
      "type": "code",
      "source": "// 3. Displaying an Interactive Scrollable Table\nbegin\n  Writeln('Displaying employee KPI performance table:');\n\n  ShowTable(\n    'Top Engineering Contributors',\n    ['Employee', 'Department', 'Commits', 'ReviewScore'],\n    '['#10 +\n    '  {\"Employee\": \"Alice Chen\",   \"Department\": \"Core Backend\",  \"Commits\": 142, \"ReviewScore\": 98.5},'#10 +\n    '  {\"Employee\": \"Bruno Silva\",  \"Department\": \"Compiler Tool\", \"Commits\": 118, \"ReviewScore\": 94.2},'#10 +\n    '  {\"Employee\": \"Carla Rossi\",  \"Department\": \"Data Science\",  \"Commits\": 165, \"ReviewScore\": 99.1},'#10 +\n    '  {\"Employee\": \"David Kim\",    \"Department\": \"UI Framework\",  \"Commits\": 89,  \"ReviewScore\": 91.0}'#10 +\n    ']'\n  );\nend;"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_6_md_next",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "Now you know how visual payloads work under the hood! In **Example 5**, we will discover the ultimate power of BlaiseNotebook: the **Pascal Data Science API (`TPyDataFrame`)**, where you create charts and tables automatically with one line of code!"
    }
  ]
}
